# ADRs
(DEC/'ADR-0001-canonical-primitive-role-authority.md').write_text('''# ADR-0001 — Canonical authority for P1–P6\n\n**Status:** accepted for Step 1.\n\nFoundations II explicitly fixes the six role meanings for its theorem chain. Therefore its definitions govern the repository. Foundations I’s labels are preserved as concrete operational realizations, not averaged into competing definitions. This prevents generic semantics→P1, generic transitions→P3, and generic paths→P5 misclassification. Directionality uses the narrower P6_drive face and cannot be inferred from P3 holonomy alone.\n\nSources: P027 lines 254–303 and 1208–1245; P031 lines 1175–1207.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
(DEC/'ADR-0002-birdint-domain-tuple.md').write_text('''# ADR-0002 — BirdInt domain tuple arity\n\n**Status:** accepted working ruling; source inconsistency remains recorded.\n\nThe controlling declaration is the body’s 19-component tuple at P026 lines 806–814, reinforced by the internal/model split at lines 1472–1478. Appendix A’s “sixteen-component” record omits `Vis`, `Source`, and `Real`; it is treated as a legacy/reduced presentation, not as the complete domain. No source text is altered. Step 2 should preserve both locations in the claim dossier and, if the paper is revised, request an explicit correction.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
(DEC/'ADR-0003-law-identifier-preservation.md').write_text('''# ADR-0003 — Preserve original law identifiers\n\n**Status:** accepted.\n\nThe F/E/G/no-go registries retain the source identifiers exactly. Foundations IV contains 52 rows from F2 through F53 with split labels F13a/F13b and F15a/F15b and identifier gaps. The repository does not normalize these into F1–F52 because that would break provenance and cross-paper citations.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
(DEC/'ADR-0004-P040-P058-version-family.md').write_text('''# ADR-0004 — P040/P058 version-family handling\n\n**Status:** unresolved canonical choice; controlled handling accepted.\n\nP040 and P058 have normalized five-word-shingle Jaccard similarity 0.687845 and share the SAU theorem stack, examples, and architecture. Their filenames and internal titles are crossed, and the texts contain substantive editorial and theorem-presentation deltas. Neither is silently discarded. They are represented as one version family with two stable IDs and hashes; downstream synthesis cites the shared result family only when both support it and records variant-specific wording separately.\n''',encoding='utf-8')
print(f'roles={len(roles)} glossary={len(terms)} aliases={len(aliases)} corrections={len(corrections)}')
